  "SUBJECTS_hosereel_coupling": {
   "label": "Hose reel: straight side coupling",
   "slug": "hosereel_coupling",
   "subjects": true,
   "ground_terrain": "Soil",
   "title": "Hose reel: straight side coupling \u2014 game art",
   "lead_html": "Owner 2026-10-15, looking at the reel in game: <i>\u201cI do wish the perspective of the hose connection for the reel were straight to the left without the perspective of seeing into the pipe. It makes the pipe look \u201cbent towards the screen\u201d and doesn't let it join properly with the hose, as shown.\u201d</i> Each row is one reel texture (4 looks \u00d7 stored/laid). <b>A</b> = plain sleeve with ring bands, <b>B</b> = hex coupling nut at the body. Only the coupling changed: the body, drum, wheel and valve are the original pixels. The new coupling ends flat at the spot the code draws the hose's end coupling (u 9/256, v 135/256) and is 42 px tall, the laid hose's own width. A mock of the hose joined to it, old | A | B: <a href=\"img/hosereel_coupling_mock.png\">img/hosereel_coupling_mock.png</a>. Nothing is installed until you pick.",
